- op: discuss  # ebb8
  at: '2026-10-03T06:42:01Z'  # ebb8
  by: agent  # ebb8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ebb8
  clock: 4  # ebb8
  nonce: ebb8  # ebb8
  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). CURRENT; root cause traced; scope wider. Title updated.\n- Repro at HEAD: document.write(s) gives host_secret->network INCONCLUSIVE \"could not classify (document)\"; eval(s) gives \"(eval)\"; window.eval(s) gives \"(window)\"; TypeScript document.writeln(s) gives \"(document)\". console.log control: confirmed.\n- ROOT CAUSE: verify_claims._adjudicate_external_modules (~3690) skips an edge only when classify_call(catalogs, ...) on the I/O catalogue hits; next comes the exact module_io_is_enumerated test, then the first-party tests. taint_sinks/ (code_execution.yaml, dom_injection.yaml) is never consulted. Nothing since 2026-09-29 changes this (b2ee3ebd65 is caveat work).\n- SCOPE: JS AND TS, all four shipped rows: eval.eval, window.eval, document.write, document.writeln.\n- Ordering hazard resolved: location.hash -> eval under untrusted_input->code_execution reads violated.\n- FIX CAUTION: skip per call by (module, name) against a taint_sinks row. Do not mark window/document as examined modules: row presence is not enumeration (INV-zubuh), and window.fetch would ride along.\n- NOT CHECKED: whether python builtins.exec/compile stay clean only because builtins is enumerated."  # ebb8
- op: discuss  # f472
  at: '2026-10-03T19:52:02Z'  # f472
  by: agent  # f472
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f472
  clock: 5  # f472
  nonce: f472  # f472
  message: "FIXED ON BRANCH 2026-10-03 (jgstern-agent/fix/dudal-withholding, commit 47952dbacf, based on the stage-2 tip 2e21275d0e; merges onto origin/dev 037f94b102 without conflict by git merge-tree). Not merged, not closed.\n\nROOT CAUSE confirmed as the premise audit traced it: _adjudicate_external_modules asks only classify_call against the I/O catalogue, then enumeration, then first-party; taint_sinks/ is never consulted, and ADR-0060 forbids an I/O row for these calls.\n\nDESIGN (stricter than \"skip the call\"): a CALL whose (language, module slot, name) is exactly a provenance-builtin row of taint_sinks/ is no longer counted as never examined, and is NOT counted as an examined negative either. It goes to the opaque-site channel a subprocess launch uses (caveat opaque_boundary): what the evaluated code or written markup does next (a fetch, an <img src> request, a <script>) is in no edge. As the sole blocker it QUALIFIES (confirmed_with_caveats), never plain confirmed. Exactness: module not marked examined (document.getElementById still withholds); community/operator sink rows never read (ADR-0061); runs after the enumeration test, so Python's granted builtins.eval/exec/compile are unchanged. And a taint claim whose OWN label reaches one of these sites by an unsanitized flow is not qualified at all: it stays inconclusive and names the site (_withhold_for_tainted_evaluation).\n\nLIVE REPRO, base -> branch (fixtures from this item's description; claims host_secret->network, boundary net_send must_not_exist, untrusted_input->code_execution):\n  document.write(location.hash): host_secret->network inconclusive(document) -> inconclusive \"host_secret data reaches document.write\" (document.location is env_read too, so the secret DOES reach the call; withheld by design); NO-NET-SEND inconclusive -> confirmed_with_caveats [opaque_boundary: document.write]; untrusted->code_execution inconclusive -> inconclusive (untrusted_input reaches document.write: DOM-XSS shape).\n  eval(location.hash): host_secret->network inconclusive(eval) -> inconclusive (reaches eval); NO-NET-SEND -> confirmed_with_caveats [eval]; untrusted->code_execution violated -> violated.\n  window.eval: same as eval, site window.eval.  TS document.writeln: same as document.write.\n  eval(\"1+1\") (no tainted flow): all three inconclusive(eval) -> confirmed_with_caveats [opaque_boundary: eval].\n  console.log control: confirmed -> confirmed.\n\nA/B, 26 corpus repos (24 with JS/TS + torsocks, bellman), 312 verdicts: 312/312 verdict values identical; 0 moved toward clean; 1 evidence change (vite host-secret-no-host-fs violated 9 -> 10, WI-fiham's respelling). Released eval sites in 10 repos (apollo-server, Tone.js, mobx, dash.js, vite, clover, pyright, jenkins [+document.write], rollup, rabbitmq): every one stays blocked by other unenumerated modules. So the corpus shows NO verdict effect; the effect is shown on fixtures only. Pre-registration and per-repo deltas: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/dudal/ (PREREGISTRATION.md, ab_diff_all.txt).\n\nTESTS: smart-test affected run on the branch, 26284 passed, 2 failed, coverage 100% on the 8 changed sources. The 2 failures are test_module_slot_hint_longer_suffix[python-writer-mycsvlib.csv], pre-existing at the base and fixed on dev by 7b56f21aba.\n\nRESIDUALS FILED: WI-lagah-dosil-fumiz-ramuf-difob-vofig-poram-ropag (Python eval/exec/compile stay silent examined negatives; a launch reached by the claim's own tainted data still qualifies). NOT CHECKED: which other sink zones/languages get rows later; the rule reads whatever builtin rows taint_sinks/ ships."  # f472
